From: HNO3Miracle <HNO3Miracle@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 23:35:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Force color for color snapshot tests

Several snapshot golden files include ANSI color escapes. OBS runs
without TERM and is not detected as CI by ciinfo, so go-snaps disables
colors at package init time and those color snapshots fail. Force color
for the snaps test package.
---
 snaps/color_test.go | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/snaps/color_test.go b/snaps/color_test.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5608490
--- /dev/null
+++ b/snaps/color_test.go
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+package snaps
+
+import (
+	"os"
+	"testing"
+
+	"github.com/gkampitakis/go-snaps/internal/colors"
+)
+
+func TestMain(m *testing.M) {
+	previousNoColor := colors.NOCOLOR
+	colors.NOCOLOR = false
+
+	code := m.Run()
+
+	colors.NOCOLOR = previousNoColor
+	os.Exit(code)
+}
